    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass including the three new postcode acceptance tests).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nPostcode support for owners, validated **only when present** and optional when absent, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md.\n\n**Contract & persistence**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (4-digit string), so it's accepted on input and returned on output for both `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a nullable `postcode` column with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so create (`BuildOwner`) stores it and responses (`toOwnerDto`) return it.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column. Also updated `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (which uses positional inserts) so the seed rows still match the column count \u2014 this was the one non-obvious gotcha.\n\n**Validation (400 when out of range/malformed)**\n- `ValidatePostcode` \u2014 a new pipeline step: no-ops when postcode is absent/blank; rejects anything that isn't exactly 4 digits; looks up the city's region via the existing `Locality` table and rejects out-of-range values against a new `PostcodeRanges` table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` (checked) + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2014 turn a rejection into a 400 with an `errors` body, matching the existing error-handling pattern.\n- Wired `validatePostcode` into both the `POST /api/owners` pipeline (after field-presence checks) and the `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline; `ApplyOwner` now copies postcode on update.\n\nAll three new tests pass: valid postcode is stored and returned, an owner without a postcode is still accepted, and a malformed postcode (`\"12\"`) is rejected with 400. Every pre-existing test remains green.",
